WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.270
One theme.

2
00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:04.930
Four kinds of part, worth 2 marks, then 5,

3
00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.230
then 8, then 15.

4
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:10.730
Give each part about a
mark a minute, and no more.

5
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:14.400
Some students write an 8-mark
essay for a 2-mark part,

6
00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.950
then run short of time for the 15.

7
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.520
So why does each part need
a different kind of answer?

8
00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:23.210
In this mission, you'll
map out your paper:

9
00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:26.030
the themes, the marks and the time.

10
00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:30.460
Then you'll test real answers and plans,
and spot the slips that cost students

11
00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:31.640
marks.

12
00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:36.130
Your mission: work out why each part
needs a different kind of answer.
